From 21a829af60a7f5c7456f1f0ff9b6b0eff0ceb738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Imre Kaloz <kaloz@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:02:07 +0200
Subject: rtc: ds1685: do not sleep in the power-off handler
Git-commit: 21a829af60a7f5c7456f1f0ff9b6b0eff0ceb738
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

Power-off handlers run from an atomic notifier chain and must not
sleep. Use mdelay() for the delay before setting PAB.

Fixes: aaaf5fbf56f1 ("rtc: add driver for DS1685 family of real time clocks")
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/sashiko-outbox-169477@kernel.org/
Signed-off-by: Imre Kaloz <kaloz@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Joshua Kinard <linux@kumba.dev>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261013120208.11268-3-kaloz@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Alexandre Belloni <alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-ds1685.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-ds1685.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-ds1685.c
index e251cb06842d..1c84c5debca1 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-ds1685.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-ds1685.c
@@ -1425,7 +1425,7 @@ ds1685_rtc_poweroff(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 		/* Set PAB to 1 in Control 4A to power the system down. */
 		dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "Powerdown.\n");
-		msleep(20);
+		mdelay(20);
 		rtc->write(rtc, RTC_EXT_CTRL_4A,
 			   (ctrl4a | RTC_CTRL_4A_PAB));
 
-- 
